        "url": "https://doi.org/10.2522/ptj.20090167"
      }
    ],
    "safety": {
      "cautions": [
        "Stop if sharp pain, a pinching feeling in the front or top of the shoulder, numbness or tingling occurs.",
        "Check the band for nicks or tears and stand firmly on its middle so it cannot slip out from under the feet.",
        "Band tension is user-chosen: pick one you can control through the whole range.",
        "Muscle glow colours and activation curves are illustrative, not measured EMG."
      ],
      "modify": [
        "Shoulder pinch near the top: raise only to about 70-80 degrees and keep the arms a little further forward (scapular plane).",
        "Too hard at the top: step on the band with one foot, or hold the band further down."
      ],
      "regressions": [
        "Lighter band.",
        "Seated band lateral raise.",
        "Elbows bent to 90 degrees (shorter lever)."
      ],
      "progressions": [
        "Stronger band or feet wider on the band.",
        "Slower 3-4 s lowering.",
        "Dumbbell or cable lateral raise."
      ]
    },
    "muscleNotes": {
      "lat_deltoid_r": "Prime mover. The lateral raise gave the highest medial deltoid activity among tested exercises (Campos 2020, dumbbells); at matched effort elastic tubing gave deltoid activity similar to dumbbells (Andersen 2010). With a band the load peaks near the top.",
      "lat_deltoid_l": "Prime mover. The lateral raise gave the highest medial deltoid activity among tested exercises (Campos 2020, dumbbells); at matched effort elastic tubing gave deltoid activity similar to dumbbells (Andersen 2010). With a band the load peaks near the top.",
      "ant_deltoid_r": "Helps, more so if the arms drift forward or the thumbs turn up; external rotation (\"thumbs up\") roughly doubled anterior deltoid activity (Coratella 2020). Scapular-plane raising may be gentler on the anterior deltoid (Tsuruike 2019).",
      "ant_deltoid_l": "Helps, more so if the arms drift forward or the thumbs turn up; external rotation (\"thumbs up\") roughly doubled anterior deltoid activity (Coratella 2020). Scapular-plane raising may be gentler on the anterior deltoid (Tsuruike 2019).",
      "upper_traps_r": "Upward rotation of the shoulder blade; shrugging the shoulders up shifts work here. Highest with the \"thumbs down\" variation (Coratella 2020).",
      "upper_traps_l": "Upward rotation of the shoulder blade; shrugging the shoulders up shifts work here. Highest with the \"thumbs down\" variation (Coratella 2020).",
      "serratus_r": "Upward rotation of the shoulder blade as the arm rises.",
      "serratus_l": "Upward rotation of the shoulder blade as the arm rises.",
      "post_deltoid_r": "Assists abduction; the lateral raise gave more posterior deltoid activity than the press (Campos 2020).",
      "post_deltoid_l": "Assists abduction; the lateral raise gave more posterior deltoid activity than the press (Campos 2020).",
      "infraspinatus_r": "Rotator cuff: keeps the ball of the shoulder centred.",
      "infraspinatus_l": "Rotator cuff: keeps the ball of the shoulder centred.",
      "core": "Keeps the trunk still so the arms are not swung up.",
      "forearm_extensors_r": "Hold the wrist level against the band.",
      "forearm_extensors_l": "Hold the wrist level against the band."
    }
  },
